course: dictionary
lesson: 279
title: An amendment is a change
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An amendment is a small change made to something to correct it or make it better. «A bill goes through readings (debates), a committee that checks it line by line, and amendments (changes) in both parts before it becomes law.» The brackets tell you that amendments means changes.
explain: Use the swap check. Put the word "changes" into the sentence in place of "amendments": "A bill goes through readings, a committee that checks it line by line, and changes in both parts before it becomes law." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: A capital A means something special. «The First Amendment to the US Constitution stops the government punishing people for what they say» is one of the numbered changes added to a very important document, the Constitution of the United States. It is still a change, but a famous one.
fact: An amendment is a change made to a law, rule, plan or piece of writing to correct or improve it.
fact: «Amendments» is the plural, which means more than one change.
fact: In school writing, an amendment is a correction you make to your work.
fact: «The 19th Amendment» gave women the vote in the USA in 1920.
fact: The First Amendment protects people from being punished by the government for what they say, but it does not mean a school or shop must let you say anything, and threats are still against the law.
exercise: «The parliament voted on amendments to the new law.» What does amendments mean here? | *Changes made to the law | Parties held in the hall | Closed doors | Holidays for the members
exercise: In a formal letter you might read «with amendments». What does it most likely mean? | With a stamp on the front | *With changes added | With a happy ending | With no name at all
exercise: «The First Amendment does not mean a school must let you say anything.» Why not? | *Because threats are still against the law | Because it only covers England | Because schools make no rules at all | Because it is a rule for shops only
test: «The committee checked the bill and made amendments.» What does amendments mean? | Mistakes that were left in | *Changes | Speeches | Holidays
test: What is an amendment in your school writing? | A type of pencil | A name for a school trip | A day off from lessons | *A correction you make to your work
exam: «The 19th Amendment gave women the vote in 1920.» What is the 19th Amendment? | *A numbered change to the United States Constitution | A type of election day | A new word for a holiday | A law about school uniform
